  "question": {
    "text": "When a coil is connected across a $20 \\mathrm{~V}$ dc supply, it draws a current of $5 \\mathrm{~A}$. When it is connected across $20 \\mathrm{~V}, 50 \\mathrm{~Hz}$ ac supply, it draws a current of $4 \\mathrm{~A}$. The self inductance of the coil is ______ $\\mathrm{mH}$. $($ Take $\\pi=3$ )"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Case-I:\n<img src=\"assets\\st0009_2e3ab480b342.png\"><br />$i=\\frac{20}{R} \\Rightarrow R=4 \\Omega$\nCase-II:<img src=\"assets\\st0009_48d547572252.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{i}=\\frac{20}{\\mathrm{Z}} \\\\ & 4=\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{R}^2+\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{L}}^2}} \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{\\mathrm{R}^2+\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{L}}^2}=5 \\\\ & \\mathrm{R}^2+\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{L}}^2=25 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{L}}=3 \\Omega \\\\ & \\mathrm{L}=\\frac{3}{2 \\pi \\mathrm{f}}=\\frac{1}{2 \\times 50}=\\frac{1000}{100} \\mathrm{mH} \\\\ & \\mathrm{L}=10 \\mathrm{mH}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}